From c0ae859aae5b9b206071ae43761f0a34637b2570 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zehrer-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:53:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] netstack: watchdog that names the call a stuck main loop is
 in

netstack runs on one thread: one call that never returns stops the whole
stack, its netcfg scheme too (redox-rpi #92). The main loop now records
which event it handles and whether it is writing to or reading from the
network device. A second thread writes to /scheme/debug when that has
taken more than 5 s, again every 30 s, and once more when the loop comes
back.
